{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"46efde36fe8d828b8c784d0a7a025477dea0fe4e62e8dbb89cabb55bb7f83532","digest":{"component_or_area":"transition gates and force semantics","key_entities":["src/rebar/_lib_writes.py","src/rebar/_commands/transition.py","src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","docs/concurrency.md","force flag","unresolved-children guard"],"problem_keywords":["force","gate bypass","ticket invariant","documentation mismatch","close restriction","unresolved children"],"propositions":["Documentation claims force can waive the unresolved-children close restriction, but CLI and implementation enforce it unconditionally.","The close-with-open-children prohibition is a ticket-system invariant, not a gate, and should not be bypassable via force.","Force should bypass all gates (including future gates) but not ticket-system invariants; current guidance conflates or enumerates specific gates instead of stating this stable abstraction.","Public API contract surfaces (Python docs, CLI, MCP, user guide, agent guidance) have inconsistent wording about what force bypasses.","Contract tests must validate that force bypasses enabled gates while maintaining the invariant that a parent cannot be closed while any child remains non-closed."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787726088177291001,"uuid":"c15797ba-ba5d-4631-a47b-147b874802eb"}